@@ -16,9 +16,59 @@ logos belong to their owners.
 - Display name DeepSeek Harness rewritten to Crew Harness in prose docs only.
 - This file and a README banner added.
 
-## Not done yet (stage 2)
+## Changed in stage 2 (gate wired and tested)
 
-- Package names, binaries, identifiers and UI strings are still upstream's.
+Upstream is a developer preview (root package.json version 0.2.1-alpha.1 at the
+pinned commit; the catalog row still quotes the older README figure
+0.1.0-rc.5). Every claim below is a claim about that preview.
+
+- Model plugin -> OpenVault `/v1`. The base bundle and the sdk-minimal bundle
+  mount one OpenAI-compatible route, `openvault`, on `dsh-llm-pi-ai` at
+  `${NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL}/v1` (default `http://127.0.0.1:5000/v1`), model
+  `auto` (OpenVault's catalog pick). New Agents and the ACP server default to
+  provider `openvault`. The direct DeepSeek rows (`llm-deepseek`,
+  `llm-deepseek-account`) are not mounted. The only credential reference in
+  the default config is `NETIE_OPENVAULT_KEY`, the caller's issued `ov_`
+  identity; no provider key field (DEEPSEEK_API_KEY and the like) remains.
+  The keyed DeepSeek search route is gone and `web_search` is off.
+- Tool and sandbox plugins register only under the Crew gate. New package
+  `packages/guard/crew-gate` (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-crew-gate`) ports the Netie
+  contract shape: `POST ${NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL}/api/crew/gate` with
+  `{kind, id, intent, parent_run_id, child_id}` and nothing else; a body key
+  (`skill_body`, `prompt`, `instructions`, `transcript`), an unregistered
+  kind, a missing URL, a transport failure or a reply without `allowed: true`
+  is a refusal. It mounts a `tools/pre-execute` listener, so every tool body
+  waits for `allowed: true`. The tool registry (`tools.crewGate: required`)
+  and the sandbox provider (`sandbox-local crewGate: required`) inject the
+  gate and refuse registration with a visible error while it is absent.
+- Names: the `dsh` help line, the `dsh web` help line, the Web GUI prompt and
+  URL description, the onboarding brand and the plugin-manager safety line
+  say Crew Harness. The official client build title says Crew Harness.
+- Upstream tests that pinned the old brand now state the new value (none
+  deleted or skipped): `apps/cli/tests/plugin.spec.ts` inline snapshot, four
+  onboarding snapshot files, the acp-app and sdk-minimal specs, the client
+  build title spec. The Cordis catalog generator maps `crewGate` to
+  `docs/subsystems/sandbox.md` and exempts the `GateAsk` type; generated docs
+  were regenerated, not edited.
+- Gate tests, in the upstream runner: `packages/bundle/base/tests/netie-defaults.spec.ts`
+  (the shipped patch files parsed and evaluated by the real loader) and
+  `packages/guard/crew-gate/tests/crew-gate.spec.ts` (the live registry).
+  Both fail on the upstream defaults.
+
+## Not done yet (stage 3)
+
+- Package scope `@deepseek-ai/*`, the `dsh` binary name, the `DSH_*` env
+  names, the `~/.dsh` home, the Desktop app and container names: each needs
+  a build and a rebase plan to rename. About 190 further "DeepSeek Harness"
+  strings sit in package.json descriptions, zh locale strings and prompts.
+- SDK code defaults (`packages/sdk/client`, `subagent-dsh-sdk`) still say
+  `deepseek-official` when a caller passes no provider; the shipped bundles
+  override them, the code constants do not.
+- The DeepSeek account sign-in platform row (`deepseek-account`) and the Web
+  Models page onboarding dialog still exist; they are not a model route.
+- Sandbox confinement calls are not posted individually; the tool call that
+  spawns them is. A `skill` kind is refused until OpenVault has a registry row.
+- Whether OpenVault `/v1` refuses a call without `NETIE_OPENVAULT_KEY`, and
+  whether it serves `/v1/models`, is not measured here.
 - SECURITY, SUPPORT and CONTRIBUTING contacts and URLs still point at upstream.
 - Translated docs, changelogs and third-party notices are untouched.
-- Netie gate wiring: Model plugin -> OpenVault /v1. Tool and sandbox plugins register only through Cortex tool_runner.
