+---
+description: "The Netie Crew gate: an ids-only OpenVault crew/gate client and the registration wrap every tool and sandbox provider mounts under, for operators and maintainers wiring the harness into the Netie estate."
+kind: "package-reference"
+---
+
+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-crew-gate
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+`@deepseek-ai/dsh-crew-gate` is the fail-closed wrap between Crew Harness and OpenVault, the single key vault and gate of the Netie estate. Before any tool body runs, the plugin asks `POST ${NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL}/api/crew/gate` with ids only (`kind`, `id`, `intent`, `parent_run_id`, `child_id`) and runs the tool only on `allowed: true`. A missing URL, a transport failure, a reply that is not an object or does not say `allowed: true`, an ask that carries a body key, or a kind OpenVault does not register is a visible refusal. The tool registry (`tools.crewGate: required`) and the local sandbox provider (`crewGate: required`) refuse to register at all while this service is absent. The package is mounted by the `dsh` base bundle and by `dsh-sdk-minimal`.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Use this package](#use-this-package)
+- [Understand the implementation](#understand-the-implementation)
+- [Further Exploration](#further-exploration)
+- [Model Experience](#model-experience)
+- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+-----
+
+<a id="use-this-package"></a>
+## Use this package
+
+The shipped bundles already mount the plugin ahead of the tool registry and the sandbox provider. Set `NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL` to the OpenVault base URL (default `http://127.0.0.1:5000`); it is a location, never a key.
+
+### When to choose it
+
+Choose it whenever the composition is a Netie product: every tool call then carries an OpenVault verdict, and a tool that cannot go through the gate is not a Crew tool. Leave `crewGate: off` on the registry and the sandbox only in a composition that does not ship, such as an upstream unit test.
+
+### Setting it up
+
+```yaml
+- id: crew-gate
+  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-crew-gate'
+  config:
+    openVaultUrl: !!js "process.env.NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL ?? 'http://127.0.0.1:5000'"
+- id: tools
+  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools'
+  inject: [crewGate]
+  config:
+    crewGate: required
+- id: sandbox
+  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-sandbox-local'
+  inject: [crewGate]
+  config:
+    crewGate: required
+```
+
+| Field | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `openVaultUrl` | empty | OpenVault base URL; empty refuses every ask |
+| `timeoutMs` | `5000` | Transport timeout per ask |
+
+### What you get
+
+Each tool execution becomes one ask: `kind: service`, `id` the tool name, `intent: tool`, `parent_run_id` the calling agent's session id, `child_id` the tool call id. The reply's body keys are dropped before it is read. A refusal reaches the model as an error result with `error.info.code` `CREW_GATE_DENIED` and the vault's reason in the message; the tool body never ran. `ctx.crewGate.allow(ask)` is available to other plugins for their own asks.
+
+-----
+
+<a id="understand-the-implementation"></a>
+## Understand the implementation
+
+<details>
+<summary>Implementation internals</summary>
+
+The observable behavior is fully covered in [Use this package](#use-this-package).
+
+### Design philosophy
+
+- **Port the contract shape, import nothing.** The wire body, the dropped keys (`skill_body`, `prompt`, `instructions`, `transcript`), the registered kinds (`memory`, `api`, `component`, `runtime`, `model`, `service`) and the pre-POST refusals mirror the Netie `crew_ov_gate.py` client so a permissive mock cannot greenwash a `skill` kind or a body.
+- **Refusal at registration, not only at call time.** `dsh-tools` and `dsh-sandbox-local` read `ctx.get('crewGate')` when `crewGate: required`; the composition rows inject `crewGate`, so neither can activate before the gate exists.
+- **No cache, no state.** One ask per execution; the vault's answer is never remembered.
+
+### Source map
+
+| File | Role |
+|---|---|
+| [`src/index.ts`](src/index.ts) | `CrewGate` service, `CrewGateDenied`, `stripBodies`, `hasBodies`, the `tools/pre-execute` listener |
+
+</details>
+
+-----
+
+<a id="further-exploration"></a>
+## Further Exploration
+
+- [Tools subsystem reference](../../../docs/subsystems/tools.md), the `tools/pre-execute` waterfall this plugin answers.
+- `NETIE-ATTRIBUTION.md` at the repository root, what stage 2 changed and what stage 3 still owes.
+- [guard group map](../README.md), the sibling guard packages.
+
+-----
+
+<a id="model-experience"></a>
+## Model Experience
+
+### Conditional tool result
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+This plugin adds no prompt or schema. When OpenVault refuses, the tool result is `Error: crew gate: <reason>` with the structured `CREW_GATE_DENIED` error; otherwise the original result passes through unchanged.
+
+#### Token effect
+
+Zero tokens on allowed calls. A refusal adds one small retained error result.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+Append-only; a refusal result follows the reusable request prefix and does not invalidate existing KV Cache entries.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>
+
+- **One ask per tool call** - every tool body waits one OpenVault round trip; there is no batching and no cache, by design.
+- **Sandbox confinement is not asked per command** - the provider is refused at registration without the gate, but each `confine()` is covered by the tool call that spawns it, not by its own ask.
+- **`skill` kind refused** - until OpenVault carries a skill registry row, an ask of kind `skill` is refused before POST.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+### Dev Note
+
+<details>
+<summary>Working context for maintainers</summary>
+
+Whether OpenVault `/v1` needs the `NETIE_OPENVAULT_KEY` identity and whether `/api/crew/gate` is on OpenVault main is not measured from this repository; the Netie TAS and its patches own that.
+
+</details>
